    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Build passes and the single test is green. The audit log now shows `M27` (consistent with the mapper) for a Sept-2026 registration date.\n\n## Summary\n\nMoved date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, numbered by the year it ends \u2014 so Sept 2026 \u2192 FY27).\n\n**New cohesive unit** \u2014 `service/FiscalYear.java`: three tiny static methods (`yearOf`, `label`, `elapsed`) with no surrounding class complexity. All the fiscal-year arithmetic lives here so the changed call sites stay one-liners.\n\n**Behaviour changes, each a minimal edit:**\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 the `membershipNumber` mapping now derives its `-M<YY>` segment from `FiscalYear.label(...)`, and a new `fiscalYear` mapping returns `FY<YY>` from the business-day-adjusted registration date.\n- `service/MembershipPoints.java` \u2014 tenure now grants +3 for over one *elapsed fiscal year* (`FiscalYear.elapsed(...) > 1`) instead of a 365-day window; dropped the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import.\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 the audit log's membership identifier (a duplicate of the mapper's formula) updated to the same fiscal-year segment, one line, so the identifier is consistent everywhere.\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `fiscalYear` schema field and updated the `membershipNumber`/`membershipPoints` descriptions.\n\n**Structural-impact notes:** the fiscal logic was concentrated in one new low-complexity class, so every function I edited changed by roughly a single line and none grew in cyclomatic complexity. The one unavoidable touch of the large controller class was held to a single line.\n\nThe `> 1` tenure threshold is a judgement call the spec left implicit \u2014 I read \"tenure over [one year]\" as \"over one elapsed fiscal year.\" If you intended \"any fiscal-year boundary crossed\" (`>= 1`), that's a one-token change.",
